# ============================================================================
#  ned5 postgui.hal  --  GUI HAL glue. Runs AFTER the nedgui screen has built
#  its HAL pins and AFTER the HAL component is 'ready'.
#
#  In this SIM config there is nothing real to wire, so the placeholders below
#  are left commented. They mark the "obvious home" for the two pending GUI
#  features. On the real machine (a future ned5 running the Mesa HAL) uncomment
#  and connect them to real signals.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (b) LIMIT-SWITCH-HIT INDICATOR  (Limits page -> LED widget "led_limit_hit")
#     The LED creates a HAL input bit pin named:   nedgui.limit-hit
#     Wire your OR'd hard-limit signal into it, e.g.:
#
#       net any-limit  <your-summed-limit-signal>  =>  nedgui.limit-hit
#
#     (Find the exact pin at runtime with:  halcmd show pin | grep limit-hit)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (a) ON-SCREEN MPG AXIS + SPEED INDICATOR  (MPG page)
#     The nedgui MPG page has stub QLabels (lbl_mpg_axis, lbl_mpg_speed) plus
#     an axis-select LED row. On the real machine the MPG data comes from
#     mpgjog.comp (see ../ned/postgui.hal). Route those pins to the widgets here
#     or drive the labels from the handler. Left unwired in SIM (no pendant).
#
#       # example once mpgjog is loaded in the real HAL:
#       # net mpg-axis-a  mpgjog.axis-select-a  =>  nedgui.led-mpg-a
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
